PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L06U6.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":6,"cefr":"B1b","unit":6,"theme":"Science Around Us","essential_question":"How do scientists find out how the world works?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1","title":"A New Telescope Is Being Built: The Passive in More Tenses","objectives":["Students will be able to form the passive in the present continuous, present perfect and future.","Students will be able to use the passive with modals (can be seen, must be recycled).","I can say \"A new telescope is being built\" and \"New corals have been found.\"","I can say \"The results will be presented next week.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين المبني للمجهول في المضارع المستمر والمضارع التام والمستقبل.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام المبني للمجهول مع الأفعال الناقصة (can be seen وmust be recycled).","أستطيع أن أقول A new telescope is being built وNew corals have been found.","أستطيع أن أقول The results will be presented next week."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"experiment","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɛrəmənt/","definition":"a scientific test to find out what happens","arabic":"تجربة علمية","example":"We did an experiment with magnets.","image_id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS1-W01"},{"word":"hypothesis","pos":"noun","ipa":"/haɪˈpɑθəsəs/","definition":"an idea that you test in an experiment","arabic":"فرضية","example":"Our hypothesis was that plants grow faster in sunlight.","image_id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS1-W02"},{"word":"observe","pos":"verb","ipa":"/əbˈzɝv/","definition":"to watch something carefully","arabic":"يلاحظ / يراقب","example":"Scientists observe animals in the wild.","image_id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS1-W03"},{"word":"measure","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈmɛʒɚ/","definition":"to find the size, amount or weight of something","arabic":"يقيس","example":"We measured the temperature every hour.","image_id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"The passive is always be + past participle. Change the form of be to change the tense: present continuous passive am / is / are being + PP (A telescope is being built); present perfect passive has / have been + PP (New corals have been found); future passive will be + PP (The results will be presented).\nWith modals, use modal + be + PP: The stars can be seen from the desert. Plastic must be recycled. The lab should be cleaned after every experiment.\nUse these passives in science news and reports, where the result or process is more important than the person: More than fifty schools have been connected to solar power. Questions: Has the experiment been completed? Is the bridge being repaired?\npresent continuous: is/are being + past participle\npresent perfect: has/have been + past participle\nfuture: will be + past participle\nmodal + be + past participle (can be seen, must be done)","examples":["A new metro line is being built in Riyadh.","Many new species have been discovered in the rainforest.","The experiment will be repeated next month.","The planet Mars can be seen without a telescope.","Used batteries must be taken to a recycling point.","The water samples are being tested in the laboratory.","The results haven't been published yet.","Safety glasses should be worn in the lab."],"common_errors":["✗ The bridge is building now. → ✓ The bridge is being built now. (Present continuous passive → being + past participle.)","✗ A new planet has discovered. → ✓ A new planet has been discovered. (Present perfect passive → been.)","✗ The results will presented tomorrow. → ✓ The results will be presented tomorrow. (Future passive → will be.)","✗ The stars can see from the desert. → ✓ The stars can be seen from the desert. (Modal + be + past participle.)"],"arabic":"المبني للمجهول دائمًا be + التصريف الثالث، ونغيّر صيغة be لتغيير الزمن.\nالمضارع المستمر: is/are being + PP، والمضارع التام: has/have been + PP، والمستقبل: will be + PP.\nمع الأفعال الناقصة: can/must/should + be + PP: The stars can be seen from the desert.\nنستخدمه في أخبار العلوم والتقارير لأن النتيجة أهم من الفاعل."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A New Telescope Is Being Built: The Passive in More Tenses”. Let’s learn the passive in the present continuous (is being + PP), present perfect (has been + PP), future (will be + PP) and with modals (can / must / should be + PP) together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U6-LS1 | A New Telescope Is Being Built: The Passive in More Tenses","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Science Club News”: Exciting things are happening in the world of science! Here is this month's news from our school science club. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Exciting things are happening in the world of science! Here is this month's news from our school science club.","visual":"Image GV-L06-U6-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"The passive is always be + past participle. Change the form of be to change the tense: present continuous passive am / is / are being + PP (A telescope is being built); present perfect passive has / have been + PP (New corals have been found); future passive will be + PP (The results will be presented). With modals, use modal + be + PP: The stars can be seen from the desert. Plastic must be recycled. The lab should be cleaned after every experiment.","on_screen":"present continuous: is/are being + past participle • present perfect: has/have been + past participle • future: will be + past participle","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. A new metro line is being built in Riyadh. Many new species have been discovered in the rainforest. The experiment will be repeated next month.","on_screen":"A new metro line is being built in Riyadh. / Many new species have been discovered in the rainforest. / The experiment will be repeated next month.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The bridge is building now.” That’s not right. We say: “The bridge is being built now.” Present continuous passive → being + past participle.","on_screen":"✗ The bridge is building now.   ✓ The bridge is being built now.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"A telescope is being built.\" Is it finished? … Think! … No – the work is in progress now. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"A new telescope is being built\" and \"New corals have been found.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"A new telescope is being built\" and \"New corals have been found.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: the passive in the present continuous (is being + PP), present perfect (has been + PP), future (will be + PP) and with modals (can / must / should be + PP).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","المبني للمجهول دائمًا be + التصريف الثالث، ونغيّر صيغة be لتغيير الزمن.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The bridge is building now. — الصحيح: The bridge is being built now.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول A new telescope is being built وNew corals have been found."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Science Club News","body":"Exciting things are happening in the world of science! Here is this month's news from our school science club.\nA huge new space telescope is being built by an international team. It will be launched in a few years, and scientists hope that thousands of new planets will be discovered.\nCloser to home, coral reefs in the Red Sea are being studied by marine biologists. Some corals have been damaged by warm water, but other corals have been found that can survive the heat.\nIn our city, solar panels are being installed on the roofs of many schools. More than fifty schools have already been connected to solar power.\nAt our school, an experiment on plant growth has been completed by Grade 8. Bean seeds were planted in three kinds of soil, and their height was measured every day. The results will be presented at the science fair next week.\nFinally, a reminder: science can be done anywhere – in a laboratory, in the desert or even in your kitchen!","word_count":170,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"A new hospital ___ in our town right now.","options":["is building","has built","is being built","will build"],"answer":"is being built","explanation":"In progress now → is/are being + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستمر المجهول."},{"q":"Two new kinds of lizard ___ in the Empty Quarter recently.","options":["have been discovered","are discovering","have discovered","discovered been"],"answer":"have been discovered","explanation":"Recent result → has/have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"التام المجهول."},{"q":"The winners of the science fair ___ next Sunday.","options":["will announce","will been announced","are announcing","will be announced"],"answer":"will be announced","explanation":"Future → will be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المجهول."},{"q":"Saturn's rings ___ through a small telescope.","options":["can be see","can be seen","can see","can been seen"],"answer":"can be seen","explanation":"Modal + be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الفعل الناقص + be."},{"q":"The experiment ___ yet. We're still waiting.","options":["isn't been finished","hasn't been finished","hasn't finished been","didn't be finished"],"answer":"hasn't been finished","explanation":"Negative / question forms of the passive.","explanation_ar":"النفي والسؤال."},{"q":"Food ___ in the laboratory. It's not allowed.","options":["mustn't be eat","mustn't been eaten","mustn't eat","mustn't be eaten"],"answer":"mustn't be eaten","explanation":"Modal + be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الفعل الناقص + be."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the passive form. Word bank: are being tested, will be shared, has been opened","items":[{"q":"At the moment, the soil samples ______ (test) in the lab.","options":[],"answer":"are being tested","explanation":"In progress now → is/are being + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستمر المجهول."},{"q":"The new science building ______ (open) by the minister.","options":[],"answer":"has been opened","explanation":"Recent result → has/have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"التام المجهول."},{"q":"The results ______ (share) with all the schools next year.","options":[],"answer":"will be shared","explanation":"Future → will be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المجهول."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"The old museum is repairing at the moment.","options":[],"answer":"The old museum is being repaired at the moment.","explanation":"is repairing → is being repaired. In progress now → is/are being + past participle.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: is repairing → is being repaired. المستمر المجهول."},{"q":"A new medicine has found for the disease.","options":[],"answer":"A new medicine has been found for the disease.","explanation":"has found → has been found. Recent result → has/have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: has found → has been found. التام المجهول."},{"q":"Safety goggles should wear during experiments.","options":[],"answer":"Safety goggles should be worn during experiments.","explanation":"should wear → should be worn. Modal + be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: should wear → should be worn. الفعل الناقص + be."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write science news.","items":[{"q":"Something that is being built in your city now: ___","options":[],"answer":"A new stadium is being built in our city.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in the present continuous (is being + PP), present perfect (has been + PP), future (will be + PP) and with modals (can / must / should be + PP) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something that has been discovered recently: ___","options":[],"answer":"A new planet has been discovered near a distant star.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in the present continuous (is being + PP), present perfect (has been + PP), future (will be + PP) and with modals (can / must / should be + PP) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something that will be launched or opened next year: ___","options":[],"answer":"A new satellite will be launched next year.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in the present continuous (is being + PP), present perfect (has been + PP), future (will be + PP) and with modals (can / must / should be + PP) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something that can be seen from your home: ___","options":[],"answer":"The mountains can be seen from my bedroom window.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in the present continuous (is being + PP), present perfect (has been + PP), future (will be + PP) and with modals (can / must / should be + PP) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A rule for the science lab with must be: ___","options":[],"answer":"Chemicals must be stored in a safe cupboard.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in the present continuous (is being + PP), present perfect (has been + PP), future (will be + PP) and with modals (can / must / should be + PP) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Science club news.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 news sentences about a science project using 3 different passive tenses.","options":[],"answer":"A robot is being designed by Grade 7. It has been tested twice. It will be shown at the fair.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in the present continuous (is being + PP), present perfect (has been + PP), future (will be + PP) and with modals (can / must / should be + PP) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 lab rules with should be / must be.","options":[],"answer":"Hands should be washed after every experiment. Broken glass must be reported immediately.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in the present continuous (is being + PP), present perfect (has been + PP), future (will be + PP) and with modals (can / must / should be + PP) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one question in the passive.","options":[],"answer":"Has the new telescope been finished yet?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in the present continuous (is being + PP), present perfect (has been + PP), future (will be + PP) and with modals (can / must / should be + PP) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin & Speak","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Work in teams of four. Player 1 spins the wheel.","Make a correct sentence about the unit theme using the cue word and the passive in the present continuous (is being + PP), present perfect (has been + PP), future (will be + PP) and with modals (can / must / should be + PP).","The team checks the sentence with the grammar box. Correct = 1 point; an extra detail = 1 bonus point.","Pass the spinner clockwise. Play for 6 minutes; the team with most points wins."],"data":[{"label":"is being built"},{"label":"are being tested"},{"label":"has been discovered"},{"label":"have been found"},{"label":"will be launched"},{"label":"can be seen"},{"label":"must be recycled"},{"label":"was measured"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The road to the airport ___, so there's a lot of traffic.","options":["repairs","is repairing","is being repaired","has repaired"],"answer":"is being repaired","explanation":"In progress now → is/are being + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستمر المجهول."},{"q":"","options":["Many dinosaur bones has been found in the desert.","Many dinosaur bones have been found in the desert.","Many dinosaur bones have found in the desert.","Many dinosaur bones have been find in the desert."],"answer":"Many dinosaur bones have been found in the desert.","explanation":"Recent result → has/have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"التام المجهول."},{"q":"A new satellite ___ into space in 2027.","options":["will be sent","is sending","will been sent","will send"],"answer":"will be sent","explanation":"Future → will be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المجهول."},{"q":"","options":["Electricity can been produced from wind.","Electricity can be produced from wind.","Electricity can be produce from wind.","Electricity can produced from wind."],"answer":"Electricity can be produced from wind.","explanation":"Modal + be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الفعل الناقص + be."},{"q":"","options":["Has the water be tested yet?","Has the water tested yet?","Has the water been tested yet?","Is the water been tested yet?"],"answer":"Has the water been tested yet?","explanation":"Negative / question forms of the passive.","explanation_ar":"النفي والسؤال."},{"q":"The patients ___ by a team of doctors at the moment.","options":["are being examined","have examined","examine","are examining"],"answer":"are being examined","explanation":"In progress now → is/are being + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستمر المجهول."},{"q":"The new laboratory ___ to students until next month.","options":["isn't be opened","won't open be","won't be opened","won't been opened"],"answer":"won't be opened","explanation":"Negative / question forms of the passive.","explanation_ar":"النفي والسؤال."},{"q":"All the data ___ before the report is written.","options":["must been checked","must be check","must check","must be checked"],"answer":"must be checked","explanation":"Modal + be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الفعل الناقص + be."},{"q":"Look! The plants ___ by the students right now.","options":["have watered","water","are watering","are being watered"],"answer":"are being watered","explanation":"In progress now → is/are being + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستمر المجهول."},{"q":"Since 2020, thousands of trees ___ in our region.","options":["are planting","have been planted","have planted","were plant"],"answer":"have been planted","explanation":"Recent result → has/have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"التام المجهول."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"The school science club's news board with three panels: a giant space telescope under construction, a diver studying colorful corals in the Red Sea, and students measuring bean plants in pots with rulers. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"The school science club's news board with three panels: a giant space telescope under construction, a diver studying colorful corals in the Red Sea, and students measuring bean plants in pots with rulers"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about the passive in the present continuous (is being + PP), present perfect (has been + PP), future (will be + PP) and with modals (can / must / should be + PP), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about the passive in the present continuous (is being + PP), present perfect (has been + PP), future (will be + PP) and with modals (can / must / should be + PP), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows experiment (a scientific test to find out what happens); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing experiment: a scientific test to find out what happens"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows hypothesis (an idea that you test in an experiment); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing hypothesis: an idea that you test in an experiment"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows observe (to watch something carefully); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing observe: to watch something carefully"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows measure (to find the size, amount or weight of something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing measure: to find the size, amount or weight of something"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin & Speak”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin & Speak"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS1-W01","script":"experiment. experiment. We did an experiment with magnets.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS1-W02","script":"hypothesis. hypothesis. Our hypothesis was that plants grow faster in sunlight.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS1-W03","script":"observe. observe. Scientists observe animals in the wild.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS1-W04","script":"measure. measure. We measured the temperature every hour.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS1-T1","script":"Exciting things are happening in the world of science! Here is this month's news from our school science club. A huge new space telescope is being built by an international team. It will be launched in a few years, and scientists hope that thousands of new planets will be discovered. Closer to home, coral reefs in the Red Sea are being studied by marine biologists. Some corals have been damaged by warm water, but other corals have been found that can survive the heat. In our city, solar panels are being installed on the roofs of many schools. More than fifty schools have already been connected to solar power. At our school, an experiment on plant growth has been completed by Grade 8. Bean seeds were planted in three kinds of soil, and their height was measured every day. The results will be presented at the science fair next week. Finally, a reminder: science can be done anywhere – in a laboratory, in the desert or even in your kitchen!","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A New Telescope Is Being Built: The Passive in More Tenses”. Let’s learn the passive in the present continuous (is being + PP), present perfect (has been + PP), future (will be + PP) and with modals (can / must / should be + PP) together. Listen to the start of “Science Club News”: Exciting things are happening in the world of science! Here is this month's news from our school science club. Look at the green words. The passive is always be + past participle. Change the form of be to change the tense: present continuous passive am / is / are being + PP (A telescope is being built); present perfect passive has / have been + PP (New corals have been found); future passive will be + PP (The results will be presented). With modals, use modal + be + PP: The stars can be seen from the desert. Plastic must be recycled. The lab should be cleaned after every experiment. Here are some examples. A new metro line is being built in Riyadh. Many new species have been discovered in the rainforest. The experiment will be repeated next month. Be careful! Some learners say: “The bridge is building now.” That’s not right. We say: “The bridge is being built now.” Present continuous passive → being + past participle. Quick check: \"A telescope is being built.\" Is it finished? … Think! … No – the work is in progress now. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"A new telescope is being built\" and \"New corals have been found.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2","title":"The Water Was Heated: Changing Active to Passive","objectives":["Students will be able to change active sentences into passive sentences in different tenses.","Students will be able to write science methods in the passive.","I can change \"Scientists are testing the water\" into \"The water is being tested.\"","I can write \"The water was heated to 100°C.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تحويل الجمل المبنية للمعلوم إلى جمل مبنية للمجهول في أزمنة مختلفة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة خطوات التجارب العلمية بالمبني للمجهول.","أستطيع أن أحوّل Scientists are testing the water إلى The water is being tested.","أستطيع أن أكتب The water was heated to 100°C."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"analyze","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈænəˌlaɪz/","definition":"to study something carefully to understand it","arabic":"يحلّل","example":"The team analyzed the results.","image_id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS2-W01"},{"word":"conclusion","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kənˈkluʒən/","definition":"what you decide after you study the results","arabic":"استنتاج / خلاصة","example":"Our conclusion was that salt water freezes more slowly.","image_id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS2-W02"},{"word":"data","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdeɪtə/","definition":"facts and numbers collected for study","arabic":"بيانات","example":"The data shows that the sea is getting warmer.","image_id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS2-W03"},{"word":"laboratory","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlæbrəˌtɔri/","definition":"a room where scientists do experiments","arabic":"مختبر","example":"The laboratory has new microscopes.","image_id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"To change active → passive: 1) the object of the active sentence becomes the subject; 2) use be in the same tense as the active verb + past participle; 3) add by + agent only if it's important. Scientists are testing the water. → The water is being tested (by scientists).\nKeep the tense! tests → is tested • tested → was tested • is testing → is being tested • has tested → has been tested • will test → will be tested • can test → can be tested.\nIn science reports, the method is usually written in the passive past simple, because what was done is more important than who did it: The water was heated to 100°C. The temperature was recorded every minute. Only verbs with an object can be passive. Verbs like happen, arrive, die and appear have no object, so (not: It was happened) is wrong.\nactive object → passive subject\nsame tense of be + past participle\nby + agent only if important\nScience method: was / were + past participle","examples":["Engineers are designing a new car. → A new car is being designed.","Someone has stolen the microscope! → The microscope has been stolen!","The teacher will mark the reports. → The reports will be marked by the teacher.","People can recycle glass many times. → Glass can be recycled many times.","The salt was added to the water.","The mixture was stirred for two minutes.","The results were recorded in a table.","Marie Curie discovered radium. → Radium was discovered by Marie Curie."],"common_errors":["✗ Scientists have found a cure. → A cure has found. → ✓ A cure has been found. (Keep the tense: has + been + PP.)","✗ They are building a bridge. → A bridge is built. → ✓ A bridge is being built. (Present continuous → is being.)","✗ The accident was happened at night. → ✓ The accident happened at night. (happen has no object → no passive.)","✗ The water was heat to 100°C. → ✓ The water was heated to 100°C. (Past participle → heated.)"],"arabic":"لتحويل المبني للمعلوم إلى المجهول: المفعول به يصبح فاعلًا، ونستخدم be في الزمن نفسه + التصريف الثالث، ونضيف by عند الحاجة.\nحافظ على الزمن: is testing → is being tested، has tested → has been tested، will test → will be tested.\nفي التقارير العلمية نكتب الخطوات بالماضي المجهول: The water was heated to 100°C.\nالأفعال التي ليس لها مفعول مثل happen لا تأتي في المبني للمجهول."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Water Was Heated: Changing Active to Passive”. Let’s learn changing active sentences into passive ones in different tenses (keep the tense of \"be\"); the object becomes the subject; by + agent; the passive in science methods together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U6-LS2 | The Water Was Heated: Changing Active to Passive","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: We measured the plants. → The plants were measured. They haven't analyzed the data. → The data hasn't been analyzed. Will they test the robot? → Will the robot be tested?","on_screen":"We measured the plants. → The plants were measured. | They haven't analyzed the data. → The data hasn't been analyzed. | Will they test the robot? → Will the robot be tested?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"To change active → passive: 1) the object of the active sentence becomes the subject; 2) use be in the same tense as the active verb + past participle; 3) add by + agent only if it's important. Scientists are testing the water. → The water is being tested (by scientists). Keep the tense! tests → is tested • tested → was tested • is testing → is being tested • has tested → has been tested • will test → will be tested • can test → can be tested.","on_screen":"active object → passive subject • same tense of be + past participle • by + agent only if important","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Engineers are designing a new car. → A new car is being designed. Someone has stolen the microscope! → The microscope has been stolen! The teacher will mark the reports. → The reports will be marked by the teacher.","on_screen":"Engineers are designing a new car. → A new car is being designed. / Someone has stolen the microscope! → The microscope has been stolen! / The teacher will mark the reports. → The reports will be marked by the teacher.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Scientists have found a cure. → A cure has found.” That’s not right. We say: “A cure has been found.” Keep the tense: has + been + PP.","on_screen":"✗ Scientists have found a cure. → A cure has found.   ✓ A cure has been found.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"They have opened the lab.\" Passive? … Think! … The lab *has been opened*. Great job! Now you can say: I can change \"Scientists are testing the water\" into \"The water is being tested.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can change \"Scientists are testing the water\" into \"The water is being tested.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: changing active sentences into passive ones in different tenses (keep the tense of \"be\"); the object becomes the subject; by + agent; the passive in science methods.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","لتحويل المبني للمعلوم إلى المجهول: المفعول به يصبح فاعلًا، ونستخدم be في الزمن نفسه + التصريف الثالث، ونضيف by عند الحاجة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Scientists have found a cure. → A cure has found. — الصحيح: A cure has been found.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أحوّل Scientists are testing the water إلى The water is being tested."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the passive sentence with the same meaning.","items":[{"q":"\"Scientists are studying the new virus.\"","options":["The new virus is being studied.","The new virus is being study.","The new virus has studying.","The new virus is studied yesterday."],"answer":"The new virus is being studied.","explanation":"Keep the tense of \"be\" from the active sentence.","explanation_ar":"حافظ على الزمن."},{"q":"\"The students have built a weather station.\"","options":["A weather station has built by the students.","A weather station is been built by the students.","A weather station has been built by the students.","A weather station was build by the students."],"answer":"A weather station has been built by the students.","explanation":"Keep the tense of \"be\" from the active sentence.","explanation_ar":"حافظ على الزمن."},{"q":"\"They will open the new museum in May.\"","options":["The new museum is opened in May.","The new museum will been opened in May.","The new museum will open be in May.","The new museum will be opened in May."],"answer":"The new museum will be opened in May.","explanation":"Keep the tense of \"be\" from the active sentence.","explanation_ar":"حافظ على الزمن."},{"q":"\"Alexander Fleming discovered penicillin.\"","options":["Penicillin discovered by Alexander Fleming.","Penicillin is discovered by Alexander Fleming yesterday.","Penicillin was discover by Alexander Fleming.","Penicillin was discovered by Alexander Fleming."],"answer":"Penicillin was discovered by Alexander Fleming.","explanation":"by + agent when the doer is important.","explanation_ar":"by."},{"q":"In a lab report, which sentence is best?","options":["We was heated the mixture for five minutes.","The mixture was heated for five minutes.","I heated the mixture for five minutes, I think.","The mixture heated for five minutes by me."],"answer":"The mixture was heated for five minutes.","explanation":"Science method → was / were + past participle.","explanation_ar":"خطوات التجربة."},{"q":"","options":["The earthquake is happened at midnight.","The earthquake happened at midnight.","The earthquake has been happened at midnight.","The earthquake was happened at midnight."],"answer":"The earthquake happened at midnight.","explanation":"Verbs without an object (happen, arrive) → no passive.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال اللازمة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Change to the passive.","items":[{"q":"We measure the temperature every hour.  (passive)","options":[],"answer":"The temperature is measured every hour.","explanation":"Keep the tense of \"be\" from the active sentence.","explanation_ar":"حافظ على الزمن."},{"q":"Someone has broken the thermometer.  (passive)","options":[],"answer":"The thermometer has been broken.","explanation":"Keep the tense of \"be\" from the active sentence.","explanation_ar":"حافظ على الزمن."},{"q":"Engineers are testing the new car.  (passive)","options":[],"answer":"The new car is being tested.","explanation":"Keep the tense of \"be\" from the active sentence.","explanation_ar":"حافظ على الزمن."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the method in the passive.","items":[{"q":"We filled a jar with water.  (method)","options":[],"answer":"A jar was filled with water.","explanation":"Science method → was / were + past participle.","explanation_ar":"خطوات التجربة."},{"q":"We added two spoons of salt.  (method)","options":[],"answer":"Two spoons of salt were added.","explanation":"Science method → was / were + past participle.","explanation_ar":"خطوات التجربة."},{"q":"We recorded the results in a table.  (method)","options":[],"answer":"The results were recorded in a table.","explanation":"Science method → was / were + past participle.","explanation_ar":"خطوات التجربة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Turn science facts into passive sentences.","items":[{"q":"Change: \"People use solar energy in many countries.\"","options":[],"answer":"Solar energy is used in many countries.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses changing active sentences into passive ones in different tenses (keep the tense of \"be\"); the object becomes the subject; by + agent; the passive in science methods correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Change: \"Scientists have discovered water on Mars.\"","options":[],"answer":"Water has been discovered on Mars.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses changing active sentences into passive ones in different tenses (keep the tense of \"be\"); the object becomes the subject; by + agent; the passive in science methods correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Change: \"The company will launch a new phone next month.\"","options":[],"answer":"A new phone will be launched next month.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses changing active sentences into passive ones in different tenses (keep the tense of \"be\"); the object becomes the subject; by + agent; the passive in science methods correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Change: \"You can see the comet tonight.\"","options":[],"answer":"The comet can be seen tonight.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses changing active sentences into passive ones in different tenses (keep the tense of \"be\"); the object becomes the subject; by + agent; the passive in science methods correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Turn a famous invention fact into a passive sentence with by.","options":[],"answer":"The light bulb was improved by Thomas Edison.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses changing active sentences into passive ones in different tenses (keep the tense of \"be\"); the object becomes the subject; by + agent; the passive in science methods correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: My experiment method.","items":[{"q":"Choose a simple experiment. Write 4 method steps in the passive past simple.","options":[],"answer":"Three cups were filled with water. Salt was added to the first cup. Sugar was added to the second cup. The cups were put in the freezer.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses changing active sentences into passive ones in different tenses (keep the tense of \"be\"); the object becomes the subject; by + agent; the passive in science methods correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence about what is being done now in your class project.","options":[],"answer":"Our solar oven is being tested this week.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses changing active sentences into passive ones in different tenses (keep the tense of \"be\"); the object becomes the subject; by + agent; the passive in science methods correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence about what will be done next.","options":[],"answer":"The results will be presented on Thursday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses changing active sentences into passive ones in different tenses (keep the tense of \"be\"); the object becomes the subject; by + agent; the passive in science methods correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Tic-Tac-Grammar","mechanic":"tic_tac_toe","rules":["Two teams: X and O. Team X chooses a square.","Using the cue, the team says a correct sentence with changing active sentences into passive ones in different tenses (keep the tense of \"be\"); the object becomes the subject; by + agent; the passive in science methods (the form in brackets: +, – or ?).","If the class and teacher agree it is correct, the team marks the square.","Three squares in a row wins. Play a second round with the grid turned around."],"data":[{"cue":"a new telescope / build / now"},{"cue":"the samples / test / at the moment"},{"cue":"a new planet / discover / recently"},{"cue":"the results / publish / next month"},{"cue":"the stars / can / see / from the desert"},{"cue":"plastic / must / recycle"},{"cue":"the water / heat / to 100°C"},{"cue":"the bridge / complete / already"},{"cue":"the seeds / plant / last week"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"\"They are cleaning the laboratory.\" Passive:","options":["The laboratory is being cleaned.","The laboratory has cleaning.","The laboratory is cleaned yesterday.","The laboratory is being clean."],"answer":"The laboratory is being cleaned.","explanation":"Keep the tense of \"be\" from the active sentence.","explanation_ar":"حافظ على الزمن."},{"q":"\"The doctor has examined the patients.\" Passive:","options":["The patients has been examined by the doctor.","The patients have examined by the doctor.","The patients have been examined by the doctor.","The patients were examine by the doctor."],"answer":"The patients have been examined by the doctor.","explanation":"Keep the tense of \"be\" from the active sentence.","explanation_ar":"حافظ على الزمن."},{"q":"\"People will remember this discovery.\" Passive:","options":["This discovery will remember.","This discovery is remembering.","This discovery will been remembered.","This discovery will be remembered."],"answer":"This discovery will be remembered.","explanation":"Keep the tense of \"be\" from the active sentence.","explanation_ar":"حافظ على الزمن."},{"q":"","options":["The seeds planted in three different soils by.","The seeds was planted in three different soils.","The seeds were planted in three different soils.","The seeds were plant in three different soils."],"answer":"The seeds were planted in three different soils.","explanation":"Science method → was / were + past participle.","explanation_ar":"خطوات التجربة."},{"q":"Which verb can NOT be passive?","options":["discover","arrive","build","measure"],"answer":"arrive","explanation":"Verbs without an object (happen, arrive) → no passive.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال اللازمة."},{"q":"\"You must wear gloves.\" Passive:","options":["Gloves must wear.","Gloves must be wear.","Gloves must been worn.","Gloves must be worn."],"answer":"Gloves must be worn.","explanation":"Keep the tense of \"be\" from the active sentence.","explanation_ar":"حافظ على الزمن."},{"q":"In \"A new star was discovered by a student,\" what was the active object?","options":["a new star","discovered","was","a student"],"answer":"a new star","explanation":"The active object becomes the passive subject.","explanation_ar":"المفعول يصبح فاعلًا."},{"q":"","options":["The bones were analyze by a team of experts.","The bones were analyzed by a team of experts.","The bones was analyzed by a team of experts.","The bones analyzed by a team of experts were."],"answer":"The bones were analyzed by a team of experts.","explanation":"by + agent when the doer is important.","explanation_ar":"by."},{"q":"","options":["The final results haven't been checked yet.","The final results haven't been check yet.","The final results hasn't been checked yet.","The final results haven't checked yet."],"answer":"The final results haven't been checked yet.","explanation":"Keep the tense of \"be\" from the active sentence.","explanation_ar":"حافظ على الزمن."},{"q":"Why is the passive common in lab reports?","options":["It's shorter to write \"I\".","Scientists don't like verbs.","The method is more important than the person.","It's always in the future."],"answer":"The method is more important than the person.","explanation":"Science method → was / were + past participle.","explanation_ar":"خطوات التجربة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A whiteboard in the lab with two columns – ACTIVE: \"We heat the water. Scientists have found a cure. They will test the robot.\" – and PASSIVE with arrows; Sara writing a method in her lab notebook next to a beaker on a burner. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A whiteboard in the lab with two columns – ACTIVE: \"We heat the water. Scientists have found a cure. They will test the robot.\" – and PASSIVE with arrows; Sara writing a method in her lab notebook next to a beaker on a burner"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of changing active sentences into passive ones in different tenses (keep the tense of \"be\"); the object becomes the subject; by + agent; the passive in science methods: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Science Around Us”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of changing active sentences into passive ones in different tenses (keep the tense of \"be\")"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows analyze (to study something carefully to understand it); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing analyze: to study something carefully to understand it"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows conclusion (what you decide after you study the results); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing conclusion: what you decide after you study the results"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows data (facts and numbers collected for study); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing data: facts and numbers collected for study"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows laboratory (a room where scientists do experiments); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing laboratory: a room where scientists do experiments"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Tic-Tac-Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Tic-Tac-Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS2-W01","script":"analyze. analyze. The team analyzed the results.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS2-W02","script":"conclusion. conclusion. Our conclusion was that salt water freezes more slowly.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS2-W03","script":"data. data. The data shows that the sea is getting warmer.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS2-W04","script":"laboratory. laboratory. The laboratory has new microscopes.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Water Was Heated: Changing Active to Passive”. Let’s learn changing active sentences into passive ones in different tenses (keep the tense of \"be\"); the object becomes the subject; by + agent; the passive in science methods together. Remember these patterns: We measured the plants. → The plants were measured. They haven't analyzed the data. → The data hasn't been analyzed. Will they test the robot? → Will the robot be tested? To change active → passive: 1) the object of the active sentence becomes the subject; 2) use be in the same tense as the active verb + past participle; 3) add by + agent only if it's important. Scientists are testing the water. → The water is being tested (by scientists). Keep the tense! tests → is tested • tested → was tested • is testing → is being tested • has tested → has been tested • will test → will be tested • can test → can be tested. Here are some examples. Engineers are designing a new car. → A new car is being designed. Someone has stolen the microscope! → The microscope has been stolen! The teacher will mark the reports. → The reports will be marked by the teacher. Be careful! Some learners say: “Scientists have found a cure. → A cure has found.” That’s not right. We say: “A cure has been found.” Keep the tense: has + been + PP. Quick check: \"They have opened the lab.\" Passive? … Think! … The lab *has been opened*. Great job! Now you can say: I can change \"Scientists are testing the water\" into \"The water is being tested.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3","title":"Observe, Measure, Analyze: Science Verbs and Academic Words","objectives":["Students will be able to use science verbs and academic words to describe experiments.","Students will be able to form the nouns of science verbs (observation, analysis, discovery).","I can describe the steps of the scientific method.","I can change \"analyze\" into \"analysis\" and \"discover\" into \"discovery\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام أفعال العلوم والكلمات الأكاديمية لوصف التجارب.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين الأسماء من أفعال العلوم (observation وanalysis وdiscovery).","أستطيع أن أصف خطوات المنهج العلمي.","أستطيع أن أحوّل analyze إلى analysis وdiscover إلى discovery."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"research","pos":"noun","ipa":"/riˈsɝtʃ/","definition":"careful study to find new facts","arabic":"بحث علمي","example":"Her research is about desert plants.","image_id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS3-W01"},{"word":"discover","pos":"verb","ipa":"/dɪˈskʌvɚ/","definition":"to find something for the first time","arabic":"يكتشف","example":"Scientists discovered a new kind of frog.","image_id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS3-W02"},{"word":"theory","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈθɪri/","definition":"an idea that explains why something happens","arabic":"نظرية","example":"Einstein's theory changed physics.","image_id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS3-W03"},{"word":"process","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈprɑˌsɛs/","definition":"a series of steps to make or do something","arabic":"عملية / سلسلة خطوات","example":"Photosynthesis is the process plants use to make food.","image_id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS3-W04"},{"word":"substance","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsʌbstəns/","definition":"a solid, liquid or gas of a particular kind","arabic":"مادة","example":"Water is the most common substance on Earth.","image_id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS3-W05"},{"word":"method","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmɛθəd/","definition":"a way of doing something","arabic":"طريقة / منهج","example":"Write your method step by step.","image_id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS3-W06"}],"explanation":{"text":"The scientific method has steps: 1) ask a question; 2) make a hypothesis; 3) do an experiment and observe; 4) measure and record the data; 5) analyze the results; 6) write a conclusion.\nScience verbs → nouns: observe → observation; analyze → analysis (plural: analyses); conclude → conclusion; discover → discovery; measure → measurement; prove → proof; predict → prediction; explain → explanation. Person nouns: science → scientist, research → researcher. Adjective: scientific.\nSome academic nouns have unusual plurals: hypothesis → hypotheses, analysis → analyses, phenomenon → phenomena. data is often used with a singular verb in everyday English: The data shows… (In formal science writing, \"the data show\" is also used.) American spelling: analyze (not analyse).\nCollocations/phrases: make a hypothesis • do / carry out an experiment • collect / record data | take measurements • make observations • analyze the results • reach a conclusion | test a theory • make a discovery • follow a method • prove a theory","examples":["Our hypothesis was that ice melts faster in salt water.","We carried out the experiment three times.","We observed the color change carefully.","The data was recorded in a table.","The analysis showed a clear pattern.","Our conclusion was that our hypothesis was correct.","The discovery of penicillin saved millions of lives.","Scientists use a careful method to test their theories."],"common_errors":["✗ We did a hypothesis. → ✓ We made a hypothesis. (make a hypothesis.)","✗ The analyze showed a pattern. → ✓ The analysis showed a pattern. (Noun → analysis.)","✗ She made an important discover. → ✓ She made an important discovery. (Noun → discovery.)","✗ We arrived to a conclusion. → ✓ We reached a conclusion. (reach a conclusion.)"],"arabic":"خطوات المنهج العلمي: السؤال، ثم الفرضية (hypothesis)، ثم التجربة والملاحظة، ثم القياس وتسجيل البيانات، ثم التحليل، ثم الاستنتاج (conclusion).\nمن الأفعال إلى الأسماء: observe → observation، analyze → analysis، discover → discovery، prove → proof.\nجمع hypothesis هو hypotheses، وجمع analysis هو analyses.\nمتلازمات: make a hypothesis وcarry out an experiment وreach a conclusion."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Observe, Measure, Analyze: Science Verbs and Academic Words”. Let’s learn science verbs (observe, measure, analyze, predict, record, test, prove, identify); academic nouns (hypothesis, data, method, theory, process, conclusion); noun forms (observe → observation, analyze → analysis, conclude → conclusion, discover → discovery, prove → proof); the scientific method together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U6-LS3 | Observe, Measure, Analyze: Science Verbs and Academic Words","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. research: careful study to find new facts. discover: to find something for the first time. theory: an idea that explains why something happens.","on_screen":"research | discover | theory","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"The scientific method has steps: 1) ask a question; 2) make a hypothesis; 3) do an experiment and observe; 4) measure and record the data; 5) analyze the results; 6) write a conclusion. Science verbs → nouns: observe → observation; analyze → analysis (plural: analyses); conclude → conclusion; discover → discovery; measure → measurement; prove → proof; predict → prediction; explain → explanation. Person nouns: science → scientist, research → researcher. Adjective: scientific.","on_screen":"science verbs (observe, measure, analyze, predict, record, test, prove, identify); academic nouns (hypothesis, data, method, theory, process, conclusion); noun forms (observe → observation, analyze → analysis, conclude → conclusion, discover → discovery, prove → proof); the scientific method","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Our hypothesis was that ice melts faster in salt water. We carried out the experiment three times. We observed the color change carefully.","on_screen":"Our hypothesis was that ice melts faster in salt water. / We carried out the experiment three times. / We observed the color change carefully.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “We did a hypothesis.” That’s not right. We say: “We made a hypothesis.” make a hypothesis.","on_screen":"✗ We did a hypothesis.   ✓ We made a hypothesis.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: What do you write after you analyze the results? … Think! … A conclusion. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe the steps of the scientific method.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can describe the steps of the scientific method.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: science verbs (observe, measure, analyze, predict, record, test, prove, identify); academic nouns (hypothesis, data, method, theory, process, conclusion); noun forms (observe → observation, analyze → analysis, conclude → conclusion, discover → discovery, prove → proof); the scientific method.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","خطوات المنهج العلمي: السؤال، ثم الفرضية (hypothesis)، ثم التجربة والملاحظة، ثم القياس وتسجيل البيانات، ثم التحليل، ثم الاستنتاج (conclusion).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: We did a hypothesis. — الصحيح: We made a hypothesis.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أصف خطوات المنهج العلمي."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"Before the experiment, we ___ a hypothesis.","options":["took","reached","made","did"],"answer":"made","explanation":"Science collocation (make a hypothesis, reach a conclusion).","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة العلمية."},{"q":"We ___ the length of the plants every morning with a ruler.","options":["concluded","measured","observed of","discovered"],"answer":"measured","explanation":"Choose the science verb.","explanation_ar":"فعل العلوم."},{"q":"The ___ of the data took two days.","options":["analyzing it","analyze","analyzed","analysis"],"answer":"analysis","explanation":"Choose the noun form (observation, analysis, discovery).","explanation_ar":"صيغة الاسم."},{"q":"Alexander Fleming made an important ___ in 1928.","options":["discover","discoverer it","discovered","discovery"],"answer":"discovery","explanation":"Choose the noun form (observation, analysis, discovery).","explanation_ar":"صيغة الاسم."},{"q":"The facts and numbers you collect in an experiment are the ___.","options":["theory","substance","data","hypothesis"],"answer":"data","explanation":"Choose the academic word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"What do scientists do after they analyze the results?","options":["They reach a conclusion.","They ask a question.","They start the experiment.","They make a hypothesis."],"answer":"They reach a conclusion.","explanation":"Order of the scientific method.","explanation_ar":"خطوات المنهج العلمي."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the word to its meaning.","items":[{"q":"hypothesis","options":["watch something very carefully","a solid, liquid or gas of a particular kind","an idea you test in an experiment","the way you do something, step by step","a room where scientists work","an idea that explains why something happens"],"answer":"an idea you test in an experiment","explanation":"hypothesis → an idea you test in an experiment. Choose the science verb.","explanation_ar":"فعل العلوم."},{"q":"laboratory","options":["watch something very carefully","a solid, liquid or gas of a particular kind","an idea you test in an experiment","the way you do something, step by step","a room where scientists work","an idea that explains why something happens"],"answer":"a room where scientists work","explanation":"laboratory → a room where scientists work. Choose the science verb.","explanation_ar":"فعل العلوم."},{"q":"theory","options":["watch something very carefully","a solid, liquid or gas of a particular kind","an idea you test in an experiment","the way you do something, step by step","a room where scientists work","an idea that explains why something happens"],"answer":"an idea that explains why something happens","explanation":"theory → an idea that explains why something happens. Choose the science verb.","explanation_ar":"فعل العلوم."},{"q":"substance","options":["watch something very carefully","a solid, liquid or gas of a particular kind","an idea you test in an experiment","the way you do something, step by step","a room where scientists work","an idea that explains why something happens"],"answer":"a solid, liquid or gas of a particular kind","explanation":"substance → a solid, liquid or gas of a particular kind. Choose the science verb.","explanation_ar":"فعل العلوم."},{"q":"method","options":["watch something very carefully","a solid, liquid or gas of a particular kind","an idea you test in an experiment","the way you do something, step by step","a room where scientists work","an idea that explains why something happens"],"answer":"the way you do something, step by step","explanation":"method → the way you do something, step by step. Choose the science verb.","explanation_ar":"فعل العلوم."},{"q":"observe","options":["watch something very carefully","a solid, liquid or gas of a particular kind","an idea you test in an experiment","the way you do something, step by step","a room where scientists work","an idea that explains why something happens"],"answer":"watch something very carefully","explanation":"observe → watch something very carefully. Choose the science verb.","explanation_ar":"فعل العلوم."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Use science words.","items":[{"q":"Write a hypothesis for an experiment with plants.","options":[],"answer":"My hypothesis is that plants grow faster with music.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses science verbs (observe, measure, analyze, predict, record, test, prove, identify); academic nouns (hypothesis, data, method, theory, process, conclusion); noun forms (observe → observation, analyze → analysis, conclude → conclusion, discover → discovery, prove → proof); the scientific method correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"observe\".","options":[],"answer":"We observed the ants for ten minutes.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses science verbs (observe, measure, analyze, predict, record, test, prove, identify); academic nouns (hypothesis, data, method, theory, process, conclusion); noun forms (observe → observation, analyze → analysis, conclude → conclusion, discover → discovery, prove → proof); the scientific method correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"data\".","options":[],"answer":"The data shows that our town is getting warmer.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses science verbs (observe, measure, analyze, predict, record, test, prove, identify); academic nouns (hypothesis, data, method, theory, process, conclusion); noun forms (observe → observation, analyze → analysis, conclude → conclusion, discover → discovery, prove → proof); the scientific method correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"conclusion\".","options":[],"answer":"Our conclusion was that sunlight helps plants grow.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses science verbs (observe, measure, analyze, predict, record, test, prove, identify); academic nouns (hypothesis, data, method, theory, process, conclusion); noun forms (observe → observation, analyze → analysis, conclude → conclusion, discover → discovery, prove → proof); the scientific method correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Name a famous discovery and who made it.","options":[],"answer":"The discovery of gravity is linked to Isaac Newton.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses science verbs (observe, measure, analyze, predict, record, test, prove, identify); academic nouns (hypothesis, data, method, theory, process, conclusion); noun forms (observe → observation, analyze → analysis, conclude → conclusion, discover → discovery, prove → proof); the scientific method correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: The scientific method.","items":[{"q":"Write the 6 steps of the scientific method for a simple question (e.g., Does salt make ice melt faster?).","options":[],"answer":"Question: Does salt make ice melt faster? Hypothesis: Ice with salt melts faster. Experiment: Put salt on one ice cube. Observe: Watch both cubes. Measure: Time how long they take. Conclusion: The salty ice melted faster.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses science verbs (observe, measure, analyze, predict, record, test, prove, identify); academic nouns (hypothesis, data, method, theory, process, conclusion); noun forms (observe → observation, analyze → analysis, conclude → conclusion, discover → discovery, prove → proof); the scientific method correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with noun forms (observation, measurement, prediction…).","options":[],"answer":"Our observation was surprising. Our prediction was wrong.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses science verbs (observe, measure, analyze, predict, record, test, prove, identify); academic nouns (hypothesis, data, method, theory, process, conclusion); noun forms (observe → observation, analyze → analysis, conclude → conclusion, discover → discovery, prove → proof); the scientific method correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with a plural academic noun (hypotheses, analyses…).","options":[],"answer":"The students tested three different hypotheses.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses science verbs (observe, measure, analyze, predict, record, test, prove, identify); academic nouns (hypothesis, data, method, theory, process, conclusion); noun forms (observe → observation, analyze → analysis, conclude → conclusion, discover → discovery, prove → proof); the scientific method correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Memory Match","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Place all cards face down in a grid.","Turn over two cards. If the word matches its definition, keep the pair and say a sentence with the word.","If not, turn them back over; the next player plays.","The player with the most pairs wins."],"data":[{"word":"experiment","match":"a scientific test to find out what happens","arabic":"تجربة علمية"},{"word":"hypothesis","match":"an idea that you test in an experiment","arabic":"فرضية"},{"word":"observe","match":"to watch something carefully","arabic":"يلاحظ / يراقب"},{"word":"measure","match":"to find the size, amount or weight of something","arabic":"يقيس"},{"word":"analyze","match":"to study something carefully to understand it","arabic":"يحلّل"},{"word":"conclusion","match":"what you decide after you study the results","arabic":"استنتاج / خلاصة"},{"word":"data","match":"facts and numbers collected for study","arabic":"بيانات"},{"word":"laboratory","match":"a room where scientists do experiments","arabic":"مختبر"},{"word":"research","match":"careful study to find new facts","arabic":"بحث علمي"},{"word":"discover","match":"to find something for the first time","arabic":"يكتشف"},{"word":"theory","match":"an idea that explains why something happens","arabic":"نظرية"},{"word":"process","match":"a series of steps to make or do something","arabic":"عملية / سلسلة خطوات"},{"word":"substance","match":"a solid, liquid or gas of a particular kind","arabic":"مادة"},{"word":"method","match":"a way of doing something","arabic":"طريقة / منهج"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"We ___ out the experiment in the school laboratory.","options":["carried","made","took","did up"],"answer":"carried","explanation":"Science collocation (make a hypothesis, reach a conclusion).","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة العلمية."},{"q":"After studying the results, the team ___ an interesting conclusion.","options":["arrived","reached","took","made up"],"answer":"reached","explanation":"Science collocation (make a hypothesis, reach a conclusion).","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة العلمية."},{"q":"Our first ___ was wrong, so we changed it.","options":["prediction","predictable it","predict","predicted"],"answer":"prediction","explanation":"Choose the noun form (observation, analysis, discovery).","explanation_ar":"صيغة الاسم."},{"q":"Careful ___ of the stars helped early astronomers.","options":["observe","observed","observant it","observation"],"answer":"observation","explanation":"Choose the noun form (observation, analysis, discovery).","explanation_ar":"صيغة الاسم."},{"q":"The plural of \"hypothesis\" is ___.","options":["hypothesi","hypotheses","hypothesis","hypothesises"],"answer":"hypotheses","explanation":"Choose the academic word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"Scientists must ___ their results in a notebook.","options":["record","prove of","discover","conclude"],"answer":"record","explanation":"Choose the science verb.","explanation_ar":"فعل العلوم."},{"q":"Before you do an experiment, you should ask a question and make a ___.","options":["substance","conclusion","discovery","hypothesis"],"answer":"hypothesis","explanation":"Order of the scientific method.","explanation_ar":"خطوات المنهج العلمي."},{"q":"Photosynthesis is the ___ plants use to make food from sunlight.","options":["theory","data","process","hypothesis"],"answer":"process","explanation":"Choose the academic word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"","options":["The researchers did an amazing discovery.","The researchers took an amazing discovery.","The researchers made an amazing discovery.","The researchers made an amazing discover."],"answer":"The researchers made an amazing discovery.","explanation":"Science collocation (make a hypothesis, reach a conclusion).","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة العلمية."},{"q":"Which word names the person who does the work?","options":["researching","researcher","research","researched"],"answer":"researcher","explanation":"Choose the noun form (observation, analysis, discovery).","explanation_ar":"صيغة الاسم."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A circular poster of the scientific method with icons: a question mark (ask), a lightbulb (hypothesis), a beaker (experiment), an eye (observe), a ruler (measure), a chart (analyze data), a flag (conclusion); Zaki the Falcon in a lab coat pointing at it. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A circular poster of the scientific method with icons: a question mark (ask), a lightbulb (hypothesis), a beaker (experiment), an eye (observe), a ruler (measure), a chart (analyze data), a flag (conclusion); Zaki the Falcon in a lab coat pointing at it"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows research (careful study to find new facts); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing research: careful study to find new facts"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows discover (to find something for the first time); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing discover: to find something for the first time"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows theory (an idea that explains why something happens); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing theory: an idea that explains why something happens"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows process (a series of steps to make or do something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing process: a series of steps to make or do something"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows substance (a solid, liquid or gas of a particular kind); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing substance: a solid, liquid or gas of a particular kind"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows method (a way of doing something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing method: a way of doing something"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Memory Match”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Memory Match"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS3-W01","script":"research. research. Her research is about desert plants.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS3-W02","script":"discover. discover. Scientists discovered a new kind of frog.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS3-W03","script":"theory. theory. Einstein's theory changed physics.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS3-W04","script":"process. process. Photosynthesis is the process plants use to make food.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS3-W05","script":"substance. substance. Water is the most common substance on Earth.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS3-W06","script":"method. method. Write your method step by step.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Observe, Measure, Analyze: Science Verbs and Academic Words”. Let’s learn science verbs (observe, measure, analyze, predict, record, test, prove, identify); academic nouns (hypothesis, data, method, theory, process, conclusion); noun forms (observe → observation, analyze → analysis, conclude → conclusion, discover → discovery, prove → proof); the scientific method together. Meet some new words. research: careful study to find new facts. discover: to find something for the first time. theory: an idea that explains why something happens. The scientific method has steps: 1) ask a question; 2) make a hypothesis; 3) do an experiment and observe; 4) measure and record the data; 5) analyze the results; 6) write a conclusion. Science verbs → nouns: observe → observation; analyze → analysis (plural: analyses); conclude → conclusion; discover → discovery; measure → measurement; prove → proof; predict → prediction; explain → explanation. Person nouns: science → scientist, research → researcher. Adjective: scientific. Here are some examples. Our hypothesis was that ice melts faster in salt water. We carried out the experiment three times. We observed the color change carefully. Be careful! Some learners say: “We did a hypothesis.” That’s not right. We say: “We made a hypothesis.” make a hypothesis. Quick check: What do you write after you analyze the results? … Think! … A conclusion. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe the steps of the scientific method.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS4","title":"You Will Need Three Things: Colons before Lists","objectives":["Students will be able to use a colon to introduce a list after a complete sentence.","Students will be able to avoid colons after verbs and prepositions, and use commas correctly in lists.","I can write \"You will need three things: a jar, water and salt.\"","I can write \"You need a jar, water and salt.\" with no colon."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام النقطتين لتقديم قائمة بعد جملة كاملة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تجنّب النقطتين بعد الأفعال وحروف الجر، واستخدام الفواصل في القوائم بشكل صحيح.","أستطيع أن أكتب You will need three things: a jar, water and salt.","أستطيع أن أكتب You need a jar, water and salt. دون نقطتين."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"experiment","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɛrəmənt/","definition":"a scientific test to find out what happens","arabic":"تجربة علمية","example":"We did an experiment with magnets.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"hypothesis","pos":"noun","ipa":"/haɪˈpɑθəsəs/","definition":"an idea that you test in an experiment","arabic":"فرضية","example":"Our hypothesis was that plants grow faster in sunlight.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"observe","pos":"verb","ipa":"/əbˈzɝv/","definition":"to watch something carefully","arabic":"يلاحظ / يراقب","example":"Scientists observe animals in the wild.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"measure","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈmɛʒɚ/","definition":"to find the size, amount or weight of something","arabic":"يقيس","example":"We measured the temperature every hour.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"analyze","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈænəˌlaɪz/","definition":"to study something carefully to understand it","arabic":"يحلّل","example":"The team analyzed the results.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"conclusion","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kənˈkluʒən/","definition":"what you decide after you study the results","arabic":"استنتاج / خلاصة","example":"Our conclusion was that salt water freezes more slowly.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Use a colon (:) to introduce a list after a complete sentence: You will need three things: a jar, water and salt. The test has two parts: reading and writing.\nDon't use a colon directly after a verb or a preposition, because the sentence is not complete before it: You need a jar, water and salt. (NOT (not: You need: a jar…)) The kit includes a magnet and a battery. (NOT (not: includes:)) …such as salt and sugar. (NOT (not: such as:))\nSeparate the items in a list with commas: a ruler, a pencil and a notebook. A good test: if the words before the colon can stand alone as a sentence, the colon is correct. Colons are also used in times: 3:30 p.m.\ncomplete sentence + colon + list: We need three things: …\nno colon after a verb (need, include, are) or preposition (of, such as)\ncommas between items in a list\ncolon in times: 8:45","examples":["The experiment needs four things: a cup, water, salt and a spoon.","Plants need three things to grow: water, light and air.","Our class studied two subjects today: chemistry and physics.","You need water, light and air.","The box contains goggles, gloves and a timer.","Some substances, such as salt and sugar, dissolve in water.","There are three states of matter: solid, liquid and gas.","The lab opens at 7:30 a.m."],"common_errors":["✗ You need: a cup, water and salt. → ✓ You need a cup, water and salt. (No colon after a verb.)","✗ The kit includes: a magnet and a wire. → ✓ The kit includes a magnet and a wire. (No colon after includes.)","✗ Some metals such as: iron and copper are magnetic. → ✓ Some metals, such as iron and copper, are magnetic. (No colon after such as.)","✗ Bring three things a pen, a ruler and a notebook. → ✓ Bring three things: a pen, a ruler and a notebook. (Complete sentence + list → colon.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم النقطتين (:) لتقديم قائمة بعد جملة كاملة: You will need three things: a jar, water and salt.\nلا نضع النقطتين بعد الفعل مباشرة (need أو include) أو بعد حرف الجر أو such as.\nنفصل عناصر القائمة بالفواصل، ونستخدم النقطتين في الوقت: 3:30.\nاختبار سريع: إذا كانت الكلمات قبل النقطتين جملة كاملة، فالنقطتان صحيحتان."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “You Will Need Three Things: Colons before Lists”. Let’s learn using a colon after a complete sentence to introduce a list; no colon after a verb or a preposition (You need…, such as…, includes…); commas between list items; colons in times (3:30) together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U6-LS4 | You Will Need Three Things: Colons before Lists","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Use a colon (:) to introduce a list after a complete sentence: You will need three things: a jar, water and salt. The test has two parts: reading and writing.","on_screen":"using a colon after a complete sentence to introduce a list; no colon after a verb or a preposition (You need…, such as…, includes…); commas between list items; colons in times (3:30)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Use a colon (:) to introduce a list after a complete sentence: You will need three things: a jar, water and salt. The test has two parts: reading and writing. Don't use a colon directly after a verb or a preposition, because the sentence is not complete before it: You need a jar, water and salt. (NOT (not: You need: a jar…)) The kit includes a magnet and a battery. (NOT (not: includes:)) …such as salt and sugar. (NOT (not: such as:))","on_screen":"complete sentence + colon + list: We need three things: … • no colon after a verb (need, include, are) or preposition (of, such as) • commas between items in a list","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The experiment needs four things: a cup, water, salt and a spoon. Plants need three things to grow: water, light and air. Our class studied two subjects today: chemistry and physics.","on_screen":"The experiment needs four things: a cup, water, salt and a spoon. / Plants need three things to grow: water, light and air. / Our class studied two subjects today: chemistry and physics.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “You need: a cup, water and salt.” That’s not right. We say: “You need a cup, water and salt.” No colon after a verb.","on_screen":"✗ You need: a cup, water and salt.   ✓ You need a cup, water and salt.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"You need: water and salt.\" Is the colon correct? … Think! … No – *You need* isn't a complete sentence. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"You will need three things: a jar, water and salt.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"You will need three things: a jar, water and salt.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: using a colon after a complete sentence to introduce a list; no colon after a verb or a preposition (You need…, such as…, includes…); commas between list items; colons in times (3:30).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم النقطتين (:) لتقديم قائمة بعد جملة كاملة: You will need three things: a jar, water and salt.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: You need: a cup, water and salt. — الصحيح: You need a cup, water and salt.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب You will need three things: a jar, water and salt."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Experiment: Does Salt Help Ice Melt? (editing passage)","body":"You will need four things two ice cubes, two plates, salt and a timer. First, put: the ice cubes on the plates. Then sprinkle salt on one ice cube. Some substances, such as: salt and sand, change how ice melts. Start the timer at 10.00 a.m. Record two things the time and what you observe.","word_count":55,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correctly punctuated sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["You will: need three things a magnet, a nail and a battery.","You will need three things, a magnet: a nail and a battery.","You will need three things: a magnet, a nail and a battery.","You will need: three things a magnet, a nail and a battery."],"answer":"You will need three things: a magnet, a nail and a battery.","explanation":"Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."},{"q":"","options":["Plants need: water, sunlight and air.","Plants need water, sunlight and air.","Plants: need water, sunlight and air.","Plants need water: sunlight and air."],"answer":"Plants need water, sunlight and air.","explanation":"No colon after a verb or preposition.","explanation_ar":"لا نقطتين بعد الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["The test has two parts: theory and practice.","The test has: two parts theory and practice.","The test has two parts, theory: and practice.","The test: has two parts theory and practice."],"answer":"The test has two parts: theory and practice.","explanation":"Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."},{"q":"","options":["The box: contains a thermometer, a beaker and a timer.","The box contains a thermometer: a beaker and a timer.","The box contains: a thermometer, a beaker and a timer.","The box contains a thermometer, a beaker and a timer."],"answer":"The box contains a thermometer, a beaker and a timer.","explanation":"No colon after a verb or preposition.","explanation_ar":"لا نقطتين بعد الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["Some animals, such as: camels and oryx, can survive without water for days.","Some animals, such as camels and oryx, can survive without water for days.","Some animals: such as camels and oryx, can survive without water for days.","Some animals such as camels: and oryx can survive without water for days."],"answer":"Some animals, such as camels and oryx, can survive without water for days.","explanation":"No colon after a verb or preposition.","explanation_ar":"لا نقطتين بعد الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["The science fair starts at: 9:15 a.m.","The science fair starts at 9.15: a.m.","The science fair starts at 9:15 a.m.","The science fair starts at 9;15 a.m."],"answer":"The science fair starts at 9:15 a.m.","explanation":"Colon in times (4:15).","explanation_ar":"النقطتان في الوقت."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Add a colon if it is needed. Write the sentence.","items":[{"q":"There are three states of matter solid, liquid and gas.  (colon)","options":[],"answer":"There are three states of matter: solid, liquid and gas.","explanation":"Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."},{"q":"You need a cup and some warm water.  (no colon needed)","options":[],"answer":"You need a cup and some warm water.","explanation":"No colon after a verb or preposition.","explanation_ar":"لا نقطتين بعد الفعل."},{"q":"We studied four planets Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars.  (colon)","options":[],"answer":"We studied four planets: Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars.","explanation":"Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"The experiment requires: two cups of water.","options":[],"answer":"The experiment requires two cups of water.","explanation":"requires: two → requires two. No colon after a verb or preposition.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: requires: two → requires two. لا نقطتين بعد الفعل."},{"q":"Bring these items goggles, gloves and a notebook.","options":[],"answer":"Bring these items: goggles, gloves and a notebook.","explanation":"(add) → :. Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → :. جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."},{"q":"The kit includes a magnet a wire and a battery.","options":[],"answer":"The kit includes a magnet, a wire and a battery.","explanation":"a wire → , a wire. Commas between list items.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح:  a wire → , a wire. الفواصل في القائمة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the experiment sheet.","items":[{"q":"You will need four things two ice cubes, two plates, salt and a timer.","options":[],"answer":"You will need four things: two ice cubes, two plates, salt and a timer.","explanation":"(add) → :. Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → :. جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."},{"q":"First, put: the ice cubes on the plates.","options":[],"answer":"First, put the ice cubes on the plates.","explanation":"put: the → put the. Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: put: the → put the. جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."},{"q":"Some substances, such as: salt and sand, change how ice melts.","options":[],"answer":"Some substances, such as salt and sand, change how ice melts.","explanation":", such as: → , such as. Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , such as: → , such as. جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."},{"q":"Start the timer at 10.00 a.m.","options":[],"answer":"Start the timer at 10:00 a.m.","explanation":". → :. Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: . → :. جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."},{"q":"You will need four things two ice cubes, two plates, salt and a timer.","options":[],"answer":"You will need four things: two ice cubes, two plates, salt and a timer.","explanation":"(add) → :. Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → :. جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write lists with colons.","items":[{"q":"Write a sentence with a colon listing what you need for an experiment.","options":[],"answer":"For this experiment, you need three things: a balloon, a bottle and some vinegar.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses using a colon after a complete sentence to introduce a list; no colon after a verb or a preposition (You need…, such as…, includes…); commas between list items; colons in times (3:30) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write the same list with no colon (after a verb).","options":[],"answer":"For this experiment, you need a balloon, a bottle and some vinegar.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses using a colon after a complete sentence to introduce a list; no colon after a verb or a preposition (You need…, such as…, includes…); commas between list items; colons in times (3:30) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with a colon about your favorite subjects.","options":[],"answer":"I have three favorite subjects: science, math and English.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses using a colon after a complete sentence to introduce a list; no colon after a verb or a preposition (You need…, such as…, includes…); commas between list items; colons in times (3:30) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Builder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The teacher reads a word and a short clue.","Teams build the word with letter tiles in 30 seconds.","The team holds up the word; correct spelling = 1 point, with correct capital letter or punctuation where needed = 1 bonus point.","Continue until all words are used."],"data":[{"word":"experiment","clue":"a scientific test to find out what happens"},{"word":"hypothesis","clue":"an idea that you test in an experiment"},{"word":"laboratory","clue":"a room where scientists do experiments"},{"word":"conclusion","clue":"what you decide after you study the results"},{"word":"analyze","clue":"to study something carefully to understand it"},{"word":"substance","clue":"a solid, liquid or gas of a particular kind"},{"word":"observe","clue":"to watch something carefully"},{"word":"measure","clue":"to find the size, amount or weight of something"},{"word":"data","clue":"facts and numbers collected for study"},{"word":"research","clue":"careful study to find new facts"},{"word":"discover","clue":"to find something for the first time"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["The human body has: five senses sight, hearing, smell, taste and touch.","The human body has five senses, sight: hearing, smell, taste and touch.","The human body has five senses: sight, hearing, smell, taste and touch.","The human body: has five senses sight, hearing, smell, taste and touch."],"answer":"The human body has five senses: sight, hearing, smell, taste and touch.","explanation":"Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."},{"q":"","options":["The lab rules are: simple and clear.","The lab rules: are simple and clear.","The lab rules are simple and clear.","The lab: rules are simple and clear."],"answer":"The lab rules are simple and clear.","explanation":"No colon after a verb or preposition.","explanation_ar":"لا نقطتين بعد الفعل."},{"q":"Where should the colon go? \"Bring three things a pencil, an eraser and a ruler.\"","options":["after Bring","after things","after eraser","after pencil"],"answer":"after things","explanation":"Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."},{"q":"","options":["We tested liquids such as: milk, juice and oil.","We tested liquids such as milk: juice and oil.","We tested liquids such as milk, juice and oil.","We tested liquids: such as milk, juice and oil."],"answer":"We tested liquids such as milk, juice and oil.","explanation":"No colon after a verb or preposition.","explanation_ar":"لا نقطتين بعد الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["Mix the flour, the water and the salt.","Mix the flour: the water, and the salt.","Mix the flour the water and the salt.","Mix: the flour, the water and the salt."],"answer":"Mix the flour, the water and the salt.","explanation":"Commas between list items.","explanation_ar":"الفواصل في القائمة."},{"q":"Is the colon correct? \"The answer is: carbon dioxide.\"","options":["No, it needs a semicolon.","No, it needs a comma.","Yes, it's correct.","No, there should be no colon after \"is\"."],"answer":"No, there should be no colon after \"is\".","explanation":"No colon after a verb or preposition.","explanation_ar":"لا نقطتين بعد الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["The bus leaves at 2:45 p.m.","The bus leaves at 2,45 p.m.","The bus leaves at 2;45 p.m.","The bus leaves at: 2:45 p.m."],"answer":"The bus leaves at 2:45 p.m.","explanation":"Colon in times (4:15).","explanation_ar":"النقطتان في الوقت."},{"q":"","options":["Our project: had three stages research, testing and presentation.","Our project had three stages: research, testing and presentation.","Our project had three stages research, testing: and presentation.","Our project had: three stages research, testing and presentation."],"answer":"Our project had three stages: research, testing and presentation.","explanation":"Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."},{"q":"Which sentence needs a colon?","options":["Oxygen and nitrogen are gases.","We need oxygen to live.","We studied oxygen and nitrogen.","We studied two gases oxygen and nitrogen."],"answer":"We studied two gases oxygen and nitrogen.","explanation":"Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."},{"q":"","options":["The kit has a magnet two wires and a small bulb.","The kit has a magnet, two wires and a small bulb.","The kit has a magnet, two wires, and, a small bulb.","The kit has: a magnet, two wires and a small bulb."],"answer":"The kit has a magnet, two wires and a small bulb.","explanation":"Commas between list items.","explanation_ar":"الفواصل في القائمة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Science Around Us” that shows using a colon after a complete sentence to introduce a list; no colon after a verb or a preposition (You need…, such as…, includes…); commas between list items; colons in times (3:30) in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Science Around Us” that shows using a colon after a complete sentence to introduce a list; no colon after a verb or a preposition (You need…, such as…, includes…); commas between list items; colons in times (3:30) in action"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Builder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Builder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “You Will Need Three Things: Colons before Lists”. Let’s learn using a colon after a complete sentence to introduce a list; no colon after a verb or a preposition (You need…, such as…, includes…); commas between list items; colons in times (3:30) together. Use a colon (:) to introduce a list after a complete sentence: You will need three things: a jar, water and salt. The test has two parts: reading and writing. Use a colon (:) to introduce a list after a complete sentence: You will need three things: a jar, water and salt. The test has two parts: reading and writing. Don't use a colon directly after a verb or a preposition, because the sentence is not complete before it: You need a jar, water and salt. (NOT (not: You need: a jar…)) The kit includes a magnet and a battery. (NOT (not: includes:)) …such as salt and sugar. (NOT (not: such as:)) Here are some examples. The experiment needs four things: a cup, water, salt and a spoon. Plants need three things to grow: water, light and air. Our class studied two subjects today: chemistry and physics. Be careful! Some learners say: “You need: a cup, water and salt.” That’s not right. We say: “You need a cup, water and salt.” No colon after a verb. Quick check: \"You need: water and salt.\" Is the colon correct? … Think! … No – *You need* isn't a complete sentence. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"You will need three things: a jar, water and salt.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS5","title":"Our Lab Report: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to plan and describe a simple experiment with the scientific method.","Students will be able to write a short lab report with the passive, academic words and correctly punctuated lists.","I can present an experiment to my class.","I can write a short lab report."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تخطيط تجربة بسيطة ووصفها بالمنهج العلمي.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة تقرير مختبر قصير بالمبني للمجهول والكلمات الأكاديمية وقوائم صحيحة الترقيم.","أستطيع أن أقدّم تجربة لصفي.","أستطيع أن أكتب تقرير مختبر قصيرًا."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"experiment","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɛrəmənt/","definition":"a scientific test to find out what happens","arabic":"تجربة علمية","example":"We did an experiment with magnets.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"hypothesis","pos":"noun","ipa":"/haɪˈpɑθəsəs/","definition":"an idea that you test in an experiment","arabic":"فرضية","example":"Our hypothesis was that plants grow faster in sunlight.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"observe","pos":"verb","ipa":"/əbˈzɝv/","definition":"to watch something carefully","arabic":"يلاحظ / يراقب","example":"Scientists observe animals in the wild.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"measure","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈmɛʒɚ/","definition":"to find the size, amount or weight of something","arabic":"يقيس","example":"We measured the temperature every hour.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"analyze","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈænəˌlaɪz/","definition":"to study something carefully to understand it","arabic":"يحلّل","example":"The team analyzed the results.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"conclusion","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kənˈkluʒən/","definition":"what you decide after you study the results","arabic":"استنتاج / خلاصة","example":"Our conclusion was that salt water freezes more slowly.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"data","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdeɪtə/","definition":"facts and numbers collected for study","arabic":"بيانات","example":"The data shows that the sea is getting warmer.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"laboratory","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlæbrəˌtɔri/","definition":"a room where scientists do experiments","arabic":"مختبر","example":"The laboratory has new microscopes.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"research","pos":"noun","ipa":"/riˈsɝtʃ/","definition":"careful study to find new facts","arabic":"بحث علمي","example":"Her research is about desert plants.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"discover","pos":"verb","ipa":"/dɪˈskʌvɚ/","definition":"to find something for the first time","arabic":"يكتشف","example":"Scientists discovered a new kind of frog.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"theory","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈθɪri/","definition":"an idea that explains why something happens","arabic":"نظرية","example":"Einstein's theory changed physics.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"process","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈprɑˌsɛs/","definition":"a series of steps to make or do something","arabic":"عملية / سلسلة خطوات","example":"Photosynthesis is the process plants use to make food.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"substance","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsʌbstəns/","definition":"a solid, liquid or gas of a particular kind","arabic":"مادة","example":"Water is the most common substance on Earth.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"method","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmɛθəd/","definition":"a way of doing something","arabic":"طريقة / منهج","example":"Write your method step by step.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 6: the passive in different tenses, changing active to passive, science verbs and academic words, and colons before lists.\nA lab report has clear sections: Question, Hypothesis, Materials, Method, Results, Conclusion. The method is written in the passive past simple.\n✔ was / were + past participle (method)\n✔ is being / has been / will be + past participle\n✔ hypothesis, data, observe, measure, analyze, conclusion\n✔ complete sentence + colon + list","examples":["The water was heated for five minutes.","The temperature was recorded every minute.","A second test is being planned.","The results have been shared with the class.","The report will be presented on Thursday.","We used three liquids: water, oil and vinegar.","Our hypothesis was partly correct.","The data was analyzed in a graph."],"common_errors":["✗ Three seeds planted in each pot. → ✓ Three seeds were planted in each pot. (Passive needs were.)","✗ We used: three pots and a ruler. → ✓ We used three pots and a ruler. (No colon after a verb.)","✗ The experiment will repeated next month. → ✓ The experiment will be repeated next month. (Future passive → will be.)"],"arabic":"نراجع المبني للمجهول في الأزمنة المختلفة والتحويل من المعلوم إلى المجهول ومفردات العلوم والنقطتين قبل القوائم.\nتقرير المختبر له أقسام: السؤال، والفرضية، والمواد، والطريقة، والنتائج، والاستنتاج.\nنكتب الطريقة بالماضي المجهول: Three seeds were planted in each pot."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Lab Report: Language in Use”. Let’s learn the passive in different tenses, active to passive, science verbs and academic words, colons before lists (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U6-LS5 | Our Lab Report: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Mini science fair: in groups, plan a simple experiment (melting ice, growing seeds, floating objects). Present your question, hypothesis, materials (with a colon), method (passive past simple), what is being done now, and what will be tested next.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 6: the passive in different tenses, changing active to passive, science verbs and academic words, and colons before lists. A lab report has clear sections: Question, Hypothesis, Materials, Method, Results, Conclusion. The method is written in the passive past simple.","on_screen":"✔ was / were + past participle (method) • ✔ is being / has been / will be + past participle • ✔ hypothesis, data, observe, measure, analyze, conclusion","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The water was heated for five minutes. The temperature was recorded every minute. A second test is being planned.","on_screen":"The water was heated for five minutes. / The temperature was recorded every minute. / A second test is being planned.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Three seeds planted in each pot.” That’s not right. We say: “Three seeds were planted in each pot.” Passive needs were.","on_screen":"✗ Three seeds planted in each pot.   ✓ Three seeds were planted in each pot.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “We used: three pots and a ruler.”? … Think! … It should be “We used three pots and a ruler.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can present an experiment to my class.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can present an experiment to my class.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: the passive in different tenses, active to passive, science verbs and academic words, colons before lists (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع المبني للمجهول في الأزمنة المختلفة والتحويل من المعلوم إلى المجهول ومفردات العلوم والنقطتين قبل القوائم.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Three seeds planted in each pot. — الصحيح: Three seeds were planted in each pot.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقدّم تجربة لصفي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Which Soil Is Best for Beans? – Grade 8 Lab Report","body":"Question: Which type of soil helps bean plants grow fastest?\nHypothesis: We predicted that the beans in garden soil would grow fastest.\nMaterials: We used five things: three pots, three types of soil, nine bean seeds, water and a ruler.\nMethod: Three seeds were planted in each pot. The pots were placed by a sunny window, and the same amount of water was given to each pot every day. The height of the plants was measured every morning for three weeks.\nResults: The data was recorded in a table. The beans in garden soil grew 15 cm, the beans in clay grew 9 cm, and the beans in sand grew only 4 cm.\nConclusion: Our hypothesis was correct. The experiment will be repeated next month with tomato seeds.","word_count":128,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the lab report. True or False?","items":[{"q":"The students predicted that beans in sand would grow fastest.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Which Soil Is Best for Beans? – Grade 8 Lab Report”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"They used three pots and three types of soil.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Which Soil Is Best for Beans? – Grade 8 Lab Report”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The pots were placed in a dark cupboard.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Which Soil Is Best for Beans? – Grade 8 Lab Report”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The height of the plants was measured every morning.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Which Soil Is Best for Beans? – Grade 8 Lab Report”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The beans in clay grew the most.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Which Soil Is Best for Beans? – Grade 8 Lab Report”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The experiment will be repeated with tomato seeds.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Which Soil Is Best for Beans? – Grade 8 Lab Report”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Three seeds ___ in each pot.","options":["were planted","planted","was planted","were plant"],"answer":"were planted","explanation":"Passive form (was/were, is being, has been, will be).","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"The height of the plants ___ every morning.","options":["was measured","was measure","were measured","measured"],"answer":"was measured","explanation":"Passive form (was/were, is being, has been, will be).","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"The experiment ___ next month with tomato seeds.","options":["will repeated","will repeat","will be repeated","is repeated yesterday"],"answer":"will be repeated","explanation":"Passive form (was/were, is being, has been, will be).","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"The facts and numbers from the experiment are called the ___.","options":["substance","method","data","theory"],"answer":"data","explanation":"Science verb or academic word.","explanation_ar":"مفردات العلوم."},{"q":"","options":["We used five things, three pots: three types of soil, nine seeds, water and a ruler.","We: used five things three pots, three types of soil, nine seeds, water and a ruler.","We used: five things three pots, three types of soil, nine seeds, water and a ruler.","We used five things: three pots, three types of soil, nine seeds, water and a ruler."],"answer":"We used five things: three pots, three types of soil, nine seeds, water and a ruler.","explanation":"Colon before a list.","explanation_ar":"النقطتان."},{"q":"What is the last section of a lab report?","options":["Hypothesis","Conclusion","Materials","Question"],"answer":"Conclusion","explanation":"Lab report section / scientific style.","explanation_ar":"أسلوب التقرير العلمي."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Plan your mini science fair experiment.","items":[{"q":"Your question: ___","options":[],"answer":"Which objects float in salt water?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in different tenses, active to passive, science verbs and academic words, colons before lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Your hypothesis: ___","options":[],"answer":"We predict that more objects will float in salt water than in fresh water.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in different tenses, active to passive, science verbs and academic words, colons before lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Your materials (a sentence with a colon): ___","options":[],"answer":"We will need five things: two bowls, water, salt, a spoon and small objects.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in different tenses, active to passive, science verbs and academic words, colons before lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"One method step in the passive: ___","options":[],"answer":"Salt was added to one bowl of water.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in different tenses, active to passive, science verbs and academic words, colons before lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What will be tested next: ___","options":[],"answer":"Next week, sugar water will be tested.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in different tenses, active to passive, science verbs and academic words, colons before lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your lab report.","items":[{"q":"Plan: question, hypothesis, materials, 3 method steps, results, conclusion.","options":[],"answer":"Q: Does sunlight help ice melt faster? H: Ice in the sun will melt faster. M: two ice cubes, two plates, a timer. Steps: plates were filled, one was put in the sun, time was recorded. R: sun 12 min, shade 30 min. C: correct","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in different tenses, active to passive, science verbs and academic words, colons before lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your report in 8–10 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Question: Does sunlight make ice melt faster? Hypothesis: We predicted that ice in the sun would melt faster. Materials: We used three things: two ice cubes, two plates and a timer. Method: An ice cube was put on each plate. One plate was placed in the sun, and the other was placed in the shade. The time was recorded with a timer. Results: The ice in the sun melted in 12 minutes, but the ice in the shade took 30 minutes. Conclusion: Our hypothesis was correct. The experiment will be repeated with colored ice.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in different tenses, active to passive, science verbs and academic words, colons before lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: passive forms? colon after a complete sentence? science words? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"We used: two ice cubes\" to \"We used three things: two ice cubes\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the passive in different tenses, active to passive, science verbs and academic words, colons before lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Quiz Show Challenge","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams take turns choosing a category and a cue word.","Grammar: make a sentence with the passive in different tenses, active to passive, science verbs and academic words, colons before lists (unit review). Words: give the meaning. Spelling: spell it. Write It!: write a sentence with correct punctuation.","Correct answers score 10 points; teams may steal a question another team misses.","The highest score after 8 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"experiment","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"hypothesis","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"observe","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"measure","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"analyze","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"conclusion","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"data","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"laboratory","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"research","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"discover","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"theory","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"process","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"substance","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"method","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The new science lab ___ at the moment.","options":["paints","is being painted","is painting","has painted"],"answer":"is being painted","explanation":"Passive form (was/were, is being, has been, will be).","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"","options":["The results have analyzed by the team.","The results have been analyze by the team.","The results have been analyzed by the team.","The results has been analyzed by the team."],"answer":"The results have been analyzed by the team.","explanation":"Passive form (was/were, is being, has been, will be).","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"\"We will present the poster tomorrow.\" Passive:","options":["The poster will present tomorrow.","The poster will be presented tomorrow.","The poster is presenting tomorrow.","The poster will been presented tomorrow."],"answer":"The poster will be presented tomorrow.","explanation":"Passive form (was/were, is being, has been, will be).","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"","options":["Gloves must be wear when you use chemicals.","Gloves must wear when you use chemicals.","Gloves must been worn when you use chemicals.","Gloves must be worn when you use chemicals."],"answer":"Gloves must be worn when you use chemicals.","explanation":"Passive form (was/were, is being, has been, will be).","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"Before the experiment, write your ___.","options":["hypothesis","conclusion","discovery","results"],"answer":"hypothesis","explanation":"Science verb or academic word.","explanation_ar":"مفردات العلوم."},{"q":"We ___ out the experiment three times to be sure.","options":["carried","took","made","did up"],"answer":"carried","explanation":"Science verb or academic word.","explanation_ar":"مفردات العلوم."},{"q":"The ___ of the results showed a clear pattern.","options":["analyzing it","analyzed","analysis","analyze"],"answer":"analysis","explanation":"Science verb or academic word.","explanation_ar":"مفردات العلوم."},{"q":"","options":["The experiment needs three liquids, water: oil and juice.","The experiment needs three liquids: water, oil and juice.","The experiment needs: three liquids water, oil and juice.","The experiment: needs three liquids water, oil and juice."],"answer":"The experiment needs three liquids: water, oil and juice.","explanation":"Colon before a list.","explanation_ar":"النقطتان."},{"q":"","options":["You: need a magnet and some paper clips.","You need a magnet: and some paper clips.","You need: a magnet and some paper clips.","You need a magnet and some paper clips."],"answer":"You need a magnet and some paper clips.","explanation":"Colon before a list.","explanation_ar":"النقطتان."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for the method section of a lab report:","options":["The water was poured into three glasses, and the temperature was measured.","I poured the water into three glasses, and I measure the temperature.","The water poured into three glasses, and the temperature measured.","The water was pour into three glasses, and the temperature was measure."],"answer":"The water was poured into three glasses, and the temperature was measured.","explanation":"Lab report section / scientific style.","explanation_ar":"أسلوب التقرير العلمي."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Grade 8 students at the science fair standing next to three pots of bean plants of different heights labeled \"sand\", \"clay\" and \"garden soil\", with a poster showing a bar chart and the title \"Which Soil Is Best for Beans?\". Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Grade 8 students at the science fair standing next to three pots of bean plants of different heights labeled \"sand\", \"clay\" and \"garden soil\", with a poster showing a bar chart and the title \"Which Soil Is Best for Beans?\""},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Science Around Us”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Science Around Us”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L06-U6-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Quiz Show Challenge”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Quiz Show Challenge"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS5-T1","script":"Question: Which type of soil helps bean plants grow fastest? Hypothesis: We predicted that the beans in garden soil would grow fastest. Materials: We used five things: three pots, three types of soil, nine bean seeds, water and a ruler. Method: Three seeds were planted in each pot. The pots were placed by a sunny window, and the same amount of water was given to each pot every day. The height of the plants was measured every morning for three weeks. Results: The data was recorded in a table. The beans in garden soil grew 15 cm, the beans in clay grew 9 cm, and the beans in sand grew only 4 cm. Conclusion: Our hypothesis was correct. The experiment will be repeated next month with tomato seeds.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U6-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Lab Report: Language in Use”. Let’s learn the passive in different tenses, active to passive, science verbs and academic words, colons before lists (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Mini science fair: in groups, plan a simple experiment (melting ice, growing seeds, floating objects). Present your question, hypothesis, materials (with a colon), method (passive past simple), what is being done now, and what will be tested next. Today you use all of Unit 6: the passive in different tenses, changing active to passive, science verbs and academic words, and colons before lists. A lab report has clear sections: Question, Hypothesis, Materials, Method, Results, Conclusion. The method is written in the passive past simple. Here are some examples. The water was heated for five minutes. The temperature was recorded every minute. A second test is being planned. Be careful! Some learners say: “Three seeds planted in each pot.” That’s not right. We say: “Three seeds were planted in each pot.” Passive needs were. Quick check: what is wrong with “We used: three pots and a ruler.”? … Think! … It should be “We used three pots and a ruler.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can present an experiment to my class.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"A new bridge ___ across the river at the moment.","options":["has built","is building","builds","is being built"],"answer":"is being built","explanation":"In progress now → is/are being + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستمر المجهول."},{"q":"","options":["A new species of frog has discovered in the mountains.","A new species of frog has been discover in the mountains.","A new species of frog have been discovered in the mountains.","A new species of frog has been discovered in the mountains."],"answer":"A new species of frog has been discovered in the mountains.","explanation":"Recent result → has/have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"التام المجهول."},{"q":"The new space station ___ in 2030.","options":["will be completed","is completing","will complete","will been completed"],"answer":"will be completed","explanation":"Future → will be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المجهول."},{"q":"","options":["The planet Venus can be see in the early evening.","The planet Venus can been seen in the early evening.","The planet Venus can be seen in the early evening.","The planet Venus can see in the early evening."],"answer":"The planet Venus can be seen in the early evening.","explanation":"Modal + be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الفعل الناقص + be."},{"q":"","options":["The report hasn't been finished yet.","The report hasn't finished been yet.","The report isn't been finished yet.","The report didn't be finished yet."],"answer":"The report hasn't been finished yet.","explanation":"Negative / question forms of the passive.","explanation_ar":"النفي والسؤال."},{"q":"\"Doctors are testing a new medicine.\" Passive:","options":["A new medicine is being test.","A new medicine is being tested.","A new medicine is tested yesterday.","A new medicine has testing."],"answer":"A new medicine is being tested.","explanation":"Keep the tense of \"be\" from the active sentence.","explanation_ar":"حافظ على الزمن."},{"q":"\"Someone has stolen the laptop.\" Passive:","options":["The laptop has be stolen.","The laptop has been stolen.","The laptop has stolen.","The laptop was been stolen."],"answer":"The laptop has been stolen.","explanation":"Keep the tense of \"be\" from the active sentence.","explanation_ar":"حافظ على الزمن."},{"q":"\"Ibn al-Haytham wrote the Book of Optics.\" Passive:","options":["The Book of Optics is written by Ibn al-Haytham yesterday.","The Book of Optics was wrote by Ibn al-Haytham.","The Book of Optics written by Ibn al-Haytham.","The Book of Optics was written by Ibn al-Haytham."],"answer":"The Book of Optics was written by Ibn al-Haytham.","explanation":"by + agent when the doer is important.","explanation_ar":"by."},{"q":"Which sentence sounds most scientific in a method section?","options":["The salt was dissolved in warm water.","The salt dissolved in warm water by me.","We was dissolved the salt in warm water.","I dissolve salt in warm water, maybe."],"answer":"The salt was dissolved in warm water.","explanation":"Science method → was / were + past participle.","explanation_ar":"خطوات التجربة."},{"q":"","options":["The accident is happened near the laboratory.","The accident happened near the laboratory.","The accident has been happened near the laboratory.","The accident was happened near the laboratory."],"answer":"The accident happened near the laboratory.","explanation":"Verbs without an object (happen, arrive) → no passive.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال اللازمة."},{"q":"We ___ the temperature of the water every two minutes.","options":["discovered","proved of","concluded","measured"],"answer":"measured","explanation":"Choose the science verb.","explanation_ar":"فعل العلوم."},{"q":"After the experiment, we ___ a clear conclusion.","options":["reached","arrived","made up","took on"],"answer":"reached","explanation":"Science collocation (make a hypothesis, reach a conclusion).","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة العلمية."},{"q":"The ___ of electricity changed the world.","options":["discovered","discover","discovering it","discovery"],"answer":"discovery","explanation":"Choose the noun form (observation, analysis, discovery).","explanation_ar":"صيغة الاسم."},{"q":"An idea that explains why something happens is a ___.","options":["method","theory","substance","laboratory"],"answer":"theory","explanation":"Choose the academic word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"The plural of \"analysis\" is ___.","options":["analysi","analysises","analyses","analysis"],"answer":"analyses","explanation":"Choose the academic word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"What do scientists usually do first?","options":["write a conclusion","share the results","analyze the data","ask a question"],"answer":"ask a question","explanation":"Order of the scientific method.","explanation_ar":"خطوات المنهج العلمي."},{"q":"","options":["The kit has: four parts a base, a stand, a tube and a clip.","The kit: has four parts a base, a stand, a tube and a clip.","The kit has four parts: a base, a stand, a tube and a clip.","The kit has four parts, a base: a stand, a tube and a clip."],"answer":"The kit has four parts: a base, a stand, a tube and a clip.","explanation":"Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."},{"q":"","options":["For this test, you need: a cup, a spoon and some sugar.","For this test, you: need a cup, a spoon and some sugar.","For this test, you need a cup, a spoon and some sugar.","For this test, you need a cup: a spoon and some sugar."],"answer":"For this test, you need a cup, a spoon and some sugar.","explanation":"No colon after a verb or preposition.","explanation_ar":"لا نقطتين بعد الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["Some gases such as oxygen: and helium have no color.","Some gases, such as oxygen and helium, have no color.","Some gases, such as: oxygen and helium, have no color.","Some gases: such as oxygen and helium, have no color."],"answer":"Some gases, such as oxygen and helium, have no color.","explanation":"No colon after a verb or preposition.","explanation_ar":"لا نقطتين بعد الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["The science quiz begins at 11,20 a.m.","The science quiz begins at 11;20 a.m.","The science quiz begins at 11:20 a.m.","The science quiz begins at: 11:20 a.m."],"answer":"The science quiz begins at 11:20 a.m.","explanation":"Colon in times (4:15).","explanation_ar":"النقطتان في الوقت."},{"q":"Where should the colon go? \"The rainbow has seven colors red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet.\"","options":["after red","after violet","after colors","after has"],"answer":"after colors","explanation":"Complete sentence + colon + list.","explanation_ar":"جملة كاملة + نقطتان + قائمة."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for a science news report.","options":["Thousands of new stars have been discovered, and more data will be collected next year.","Thousands of new stars were discover, and more data is collect next year.","Thousands of new stars has been discovered, and more data will been collected next year.","Thousands of new stars have discovered, and more data will collect next year."],"answer":"Thousands of new stars have been discovered, and more data will be collected next year.","explanation":"Recent result → has/have been + past participle.","explanation_ar":"التام المجهول."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"the results will presented at: 9:00 a.m.\"","options":["The results will presented at 9:00 a.m.","The results will be presented at 9:00 a.m.","The results will be presented at: 9:00 a.m.","the results will be presented at 9:00 a.m."],"answer":"The results will be presented at 9:00 a.m.","explanation":"Future → will be + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستقبل المجهول."},{"q":"Has the new museum been opened yet? – ___","options":["No, it's still being built.","No, it still been built.","No, it's still building.","No, it's still be built."],"answer":"No, it's still being built.","explanation":"In progress now → is/are being + past participle.","explanation_ar":"المستمر المجهول."}],"theme_ar":"العلم من حولنا","essential_question_ar":"كيف يكتشف العلماء طريقة عمل العالم؟","can_do":"I can describe science news, experiments and processes with the passive in different tenses, change active sentences into passive ones, use science verbs and academic words, and introduce lists with a colon.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أصف أخبار العلوم والتجارب والعمليات بالمبني للمجهول في أزمنة مختلفة، وأحوّل الجمل المبنية للمعلوم إلى مبنية للمجهول، وأستخدم أفعال العلوم والكلمات الأكاديمية، وأقدّم القوائم بالنقطتين."});
